# Chapter 3 — Ships & ISK

## 🚢 Ship Progression

<div align="center">
<img src="https://images.evetech.net/types/24698/render?size=256" alt="The Drake — every new player's milestone ship" width="280" />
</div>



### The Ship Size Ladder

```
Rookie Ship (free)
    |
Frigate (T1) → Destroyer (T1)
    |               |
Cruiser (T1)    Interdictor / Command Destroyer
    |
Battlecruiser (T1) → Command Ship (T2)
    |
Battleship (T1)
    |
Capital Ships (Carrier, Dreadnought, Force Auxiliary, Supercarrier, Titan)
```

### Tech Levels Explained

| Tech Level | Description | Cost Range |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Basic ships — cheap, accessible, good starting point | 1M – 100M ISK |
| T2 | Specialised, powerful, require advanced skills | 30M – 500M ISK |
| Faction/Pirate | Enhanced T1 stats, rare drops or LP purchases | 50M – 1B+ ISK |
| T3 Cruiser (Strategic) | Modular, extremely powerful, can lose skills on death | 500M – 2B+ ISK |
| T3 Destroyer | Flexible role destroyer | 50M – 200M ISK |
| Capital | Only in null/low sec, massive power | 5B – 100B+ ISK |

### Recommended Progression Path

**Phase 1 — New Player (0–30 days)**
- Frigate → Destroyer → Cruiser
- Stay in T1, learn your weapons and tank
- Suggested: Caldari Drake path or Gallente Vexor path

**Phase 2 — Getting Comfortable (1–3 months)**
- T1 Battlecruiser (Drake, Hurricane, Prophecy, Myrmidon)
- Start exploring T2 modules (they matter more than T2 ships)
- Consider faction frigates for PvP (Dramiel, Worm, Garmur)

**Phase 3 — Serious ISK (3–6 months)**
- T1 Battleship for L4 missions
- HAC (Heavy Assault Cruiser) for PvP
- Consider Marauder or T3 Cruiser for endgame PvE

**Phase 4 — Endgame (6 months+)**
- Marauders (Golem, Paladin, Vargur, Kronos) for maximum L4/Abyss income
- T3 Strategic Cruisers
- Capital ships (requires corporation support)

